VERDICT: APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS
The diff is broadly aligned with the admin UI/UX overhaul goals and does not introduce blocking functional regressions; key upgrades (dark-mode table headers via `thead-modern`, mobile filter layouts + reset actions, SweetAlert color standardization, reports chart re-init on theme toggle, chat UI/scroll behavior, video-call iframe sizing, and certificate expiry/lifetime UX) are implemented correctly.

Critical findings / analysis:
- `layouts/app.blade.php` adds a coherent micro-animation system, improved dark-mode coverage for core Bootstrap elements, fluid typography, mobile overlay polish, and reusable mobile table row-expand behavior. These are high-impact global improvements.
- Reports page chart handling is improved: existing charts are destroyed/recreated on `themechange`, avoiding stale light/dark rendering.
- Certificates page now enforces client-side expiry-date ordering and supports “seumur hidup” toggle disabling expiry input, matching expected UX.
- Multiple CRUD pages now include functional reset-filter buttons and mobile-friendly filter grid adjustments.
- Messages page improvements (bubble styling, scroll-to-bottom button, active pane structure) are good, and prior `chatActive` display issue remains fixed.

Non-blocking concerns:
1) Some AJAX error paths still silently swallow failures (e.g., `messages/loadMessages` `.catch(() => {})`), which conflicts with the bug-sweep goal of user-visible error toasts.
2) Accessibility is improved but not fully complete in changed snippets: several icon-only buttons still rely on `title` without explicit `aria-label` (e.g., some utility controls). This is polish-level, not a blocker.
3) `MutationObserver` for mobile row expansion observes all `tbody` elements globally; acceptable, but should be monitored for performance on very large dynamic tables.

Security: none observed (no new critical authz/injection/secrets risks introduced by this diff).

Next actions:
1) Add consistent error toast handling in remaining fetch `.catch` paths (especially polling/chat and CRUD async actions).
2) Do a final accessibility pass for icon-only controls to ensure universal `aria-label` coverage.
3) Smoke-test mobile row-expand on all large AJAX tables to confirm no duplicate/detail-row edge cases under rapid re-rendering.VERDICT: APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS
